BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Open Sewing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260831T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260831T140000
DTSTAMP:20260821T134432Z
UID:smcl-6a6bb887f4e5db3d00c571be@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for open time to use the library’s sewing machines. 
 Bring your own project or pick from previous library sewing projects. Need
 les\, thread\, iron\, and cutting tools are provided for use in the librar
 y. No fabric is provided except for scraps. This program is intended for i
 ndividuals who can independently use the sewing machines. There will be n
 o formal instruction.\n\n\nThis program is open only to adults 18+.\n\nNo 
 registration required\, as time and space permit.\n\nAges: Adult program (
 kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: none\nSo
 urce: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a6bb887f4e5db3d00c571be\nLast
  synced: 2026-08-21 06:44 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a6bb887f4e5db3d00c571be
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Etegami (絵手紙) Painting: The Art of Joyful Imperfection
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T150000
DTSTAMP:20260821T134432Z
UID:smcl-6a7250e7cca66c2f00a834e5@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Discover Etegami (絵手紙)\, the beloved Japanese folk art o
 f creating and gifting hand-painted postcards. Here\, imperfection isn’t
  just allowed—it’s the goal! Join certified Etegami instructors Amy an
 d Andy for a hands-on\, two-hour introduction to this rich\, liberating wo
 rld of Japanese hand-painted picture-letters.\n\nYou’ll learn to use tra
 ditional sumi ink and gansai watercolors to capture seasonal objects on wa
 shi paper\, pairing bold ink lines and bright colors with simple\, heartfe
 lt messages. Etegami is a restorative\, mindful practice designed for anyo
 ne looking to slow down and enjoy a welcoming creative space.\n\nExperienc
 e a charming side of Japanese art and leave with several finished pieces o
 f unique postcard art ready to brighten someone's day. All skill levels we
 lcome\, especially beginners. Intended for adults and seniors. All materia
 ls provided!\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not desig
 ned for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.
 com/events/6a7250e7cca66c2f00a834e5\nLast synced: 2026-08-21 06:44 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a7250e7cca66c2f00a834e5
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] It's Sew Easy: Mini-Tote
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260823T140000
DTSTAMP:20260821T134432Z
UID:smcl-6a5e85b41bbbb30f3e80a699@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Interested in picking up the fun life skill of sewing? Missed 
 out on those cute mini totes from a certain popular grocery chain? Now is 
 your chance to make your very own Mini-Tote.\n\nWhether you're a beginner 
 or experienced sewist\, this project is perfect for learning how to upcycl
 e materials. You'll also get hands-on experience cutting pattern pieces\, 
 sewing straight stitches\, pressing seams\, and more. This program is open
  only to adults 18+.\n\nSpace is limited\, so please register here to rese
 rve your spot. This same program is also offered on August 9. The two ses
 sions are identical\, so please only sign up for one. We will start lettin
 g participants in no earlier than the start time.\n\nAges: Adult program (
 kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: required
 \nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a5e85b41bbbb30f3e80a699\n
 Last synced: 2026-08-21 06:44 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a5e85b41bbbb30f3e80a699
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Embroidery for Beginners: Mid-Autumn Lanterns
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260902T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260902T133000
DTSTAMP:20260821T134432Z
UID:smcl-6a7647700d65ac36004528cc@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the Mid-Autumn Festival and learn a new skill in thi
 s beginner-friendly hand embroidery workshop! In this 2-hour class\, you w
 ill learn all the skills and techniques you'll need to complete an all new
  embroidery project by Tiffany from Stitches By Tiff.\n\nDue to high deman
 d\, we ask that community members sign up for a single occurrence of this 
 series so that as many community members as possible can participate in th
 is experience. \n\nRegistration is required to attend\, and it opens on W
 ednesday\, August 19 at 10:00 am.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to 
 tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: https:
 //smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a7647700d65ac36004528cc\nLast synced: 202
 6-08-21 06:44 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a7647700d65ac36004528cc
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Light of the Moon: Mid-Autumn Calligraphy Lantern
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T113000
DTSTAMP:20260821T134432Z
UID:smcl-6a72511788e9bf2800357fdd@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the Mid-Autumn Festival through art and culture! Par
 ticipants will learn basic Chinese calligraphy brush techniques and discov
 er the festival’s traditions. We will explore the customs and symbolism 
 of the Mid-Autumn Festival\, then practice writing auspicious phrases rela
 ted to the moon and reunion. Each participant will create a unique fan-sha
 ped paper lantern\, beautifully decorated with their own brushwork — a p
 erfect piece to take home and enjoy during the festival evening.\n\nRegist
 ration will open October 4 at 10:00 AM.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welc
 ome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource:
  https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a72511788e9bf2800357fdd\nLast sync
 ed: 2026-08-21 06:44 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a72511788e9bf2800357fdd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Financial Wellness Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T193000
DTSTAMP:20260821T134432Z
UID:smcl-6a29f9ab16554cd59fc7e57a@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join the Financial Wellness Book Club hosted by Atherton Libra
 ry and the San Mateo County Commission on the Status of Women. This summer
 \, we’re reading Make Money Move by Lauren Simmons and inviting communit
 y members to reflect on financial wellness\, confidence\, and healthier mo
 ney habits before gathering for a welcoming community conversation on Sept
 ember 10\, 6:00 PM - 7:30 PM. Together\, we hope to build a supportive spa
 ce where everyone feels encouraged to learn\, reflect\, and share perspect
 ives. Please join us!\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, 
 not designed for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibli
 ocommons.com/events/6a29f9ab16554cd59fc7e57a\nLast synced: 2026-08-21 06:4
 4 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a29f9ab16554cd59fc7e57a
END:VEVENT
